# WorkMates Inbox (React)

A React + Vite + Tailwind rebuild of the WorkMates Streamlit dashboard —
same backend, same endpoints, a SaaS-style UI (sidebar nav, light theme,
card layout) instead of the Streamlit widgets.

## Setup

```bash
npm install
cp .env.example .env   # edit VITE_API_URL if your backend isn't on :8000
npm run dev
```

Open the printed local URL (default `http://localhost:5173`).

## Backend contract

This app expects the same FastAPI backend the Streamlit app talked to,
at `VITE_API_URL` (defaults to `http://localhost:8000`):

- `GET  /emails/pending`               → `{ pending: [...] }`
- `GET  /emails/processed?limit=20`    → `{ emails: [...] }`
- `GET  /emails/stats`                 → `{ total_today, need_attention, pending_approval, total_processed }`
- `GET  /emails/log-only?limit=30`     → `{ emails: [...] }`
- `POST /emails/{thread_id}/approve`
- `POST /emails/{thread_id}/edit`      body: `{ edited_reply }`
- `POST /emails/{thread_id}/regenerate` body: `{ feedback }`
- `POST /emails/{gmail_id}/summarize`  → `{ summary, scores: { final }, attempts, tokens_used }`

If your backend runs on a different host/port, or you open this app from
a different origin, make sure CORS is enabled on the backend for that origin.

## Structure

```
src/
  api.js                 // fetch helpers, mirrors the Streamlit app's API calls
  App.jsx                // layout + tab state + data loading
  components/
    Sidebar.jsx           // nav + live pipeline status (signature element)
    Topbar.jsx
    Badge.jsx              // priority / intent / status pills
    StatCard.jsx
    PendingCard.jsx        // approve / edit / regenerate flow
    InboxTab.jsx + InboxCard.jsx
    LogTab.jsx              // auto-logged emails (OTP, promos, etc.)
    Insights.jsx
```

## Design notes

- Font pairing: Manrope (headings) + Inter (body) + JetBrains Mono (ids/timestamps/pipeline).
- Accent: indigo `#5850EC`. Priority colors: high `#E0483F`, medium `#DA8C1F`, low `#1E9E6B`.
- The sidebar's "Pipeline" panel is a lightweight nod to the original
  subtitle (`LangGraph · Celery · Redis · Supabase · Gmail`) — a small
  live-status touch rather than decoration.
